  "raw": {
    "pillar": "Climate & Environment",
    "headline": "Can a tiny turtle survive a 5,000-mile journey home? This rescue story has the whole world rooting for him.",
    "challenge": "When Rhossi, a critically endangered Kemp's Ridley sea turtle, was found cold-stunned and near death on an Anglesey beach, his chances of survival were slim. Kemp's Ridley turtles are one of the world's most endangered species, with breeding populations largely confined to the Gulf of Mexico.",
    "solution": "After two years of dedicated care at the Anglesey Sea Zoo, Rhossi is ready to embark on a remarkable 5,000-mile journey back to his natural home. A team of international conservationists, volunteers, and experts have come together to make this happen.",
    "resultHeading": "Rhossi is set to be released into the Gulf of Mexico on August 18.",
    "resultLine": "This incredible journey highlights the power of international collaboration in wildlife conservation — follow Rhossi's story at the link in bio.",
    "whyMatters": "Rhossi's story is a beacon of hope for endangered species. Every healthy adult returned to the wild strengthens the fragile population, ensuring the survival of this critically endangered species for future generations.",
    "engagementQuestion": "What’s the most incredible wildlife rescue story you’ve ever heard?",
    "captionLead": "Meet Rhossi, a tiny Kemp's Ridley sea turtle who beat the odds! After two years of care in Wales, he's embarking on a 5,000-mile journey back to the Gulf of Mexico. This is a story of hope, international collaboration, and the power of conservation.",
    "storyHashtag": "WildlifeConservation",
    "sources": [
      "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c62vd6j5llgo",
      "https://www.dailypost.co.uk/news/north-wales-news/critically-endangered-turtle-rescued-anglesey-34400577",
      "https://nation.cymru/news/critically-endangered-turtle-to-return-home-after-two-year-rehab-in-wales/",
      "https://www.northwaleschronicle.co.uk/news/26436783.rhossi-kemps-ridley-turtle-head-home-mexico/"
    ],
    "originalSource": "BBC News",
    "researchBrief": "Rhossi, a critically endangered Kemp's Ridley sea turtle, was rescued from an Anglesey beach in December 2023. He was cold-stunned and near death but was nursed back to health at the Anglesey Sea Zoo. The zoo, along with international partners, is coordinating his 5,000-mile journey back to the Gulf of Mexico. The journey involves a helicopter ride to Heathrow, a cargo flight to Houston, and a road trip to the release site near Padre Island National Seashore. Rhossi's story has been covered by multiple sources, including North Wales Live, Nation.cymru, BBC Newsround, and North Wales Chronicle. All sources confirm the details of Rhossi's rescue, rehabilitation, and the upcoming journey. The exact number of conservation partners involved is not specified, but it is clear that a significant international effort is underway. The release date is confirmed as August 18, 2024."
